                <pb facs="0490" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg382"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Quincy to Mr.
                            Durham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 119.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have read with gratification your No. 194
                    of April 12 reporting the settlement of the Mevs case by a payment from the
                    Haitian Government of $6,000 United States currency to your legation, which you
                    have paid to Mr. Mevs.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josiah Quincy</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
